  "limitations": [
    "The 88-case survey is a feature sample, not a compatibility percentage.",
    "Window execution currently supports source-free or single-source ungrouped SELECT reads, including admitted derived/CTE materialization; joins, grouped/compound combinations and INSERT SELECT windows need further work.",
    "Explicit RANGE/GROUPS, EXCLUDE, named windows and additional built-in window functions remain unsupported.",
    "SUM/AVG/TOTAL use inverse state. Other aggregate windows currently recompute frames; volatile argument evaluation, complete error-prefix timing and JSON subtype propagation are not established.",
    "The legacy fixture explicitly retains historical window lowering. Differential tests use the public Core executables with preserved and checked OVER syntax.",
    "Registered contracts cover ordering-list length, null inverse and read-state preservation, not whole SQL-window equivalence.",
    "Broader SQL, schema, rollback-file and WAL limitations remain."
